> Werethings are rather common in the early game.
> Wargs don't usually start showing up until somwhat
> later.  I've met wererats on VERY early dungeon
> levels, when playing as a Tourist with very little
> experience yet.  A warg at that point would most
> certainly be fatal.

Yes. Monsters are (mostly) created with a difficulty appropriate
for the character (experience level, dungeon depth). They are no
out-of-depth danger, or especially bad (using special attacks or
something like that). So it's certainly irrelevant whether a warg
would kill a level 1 character. Though we have to consider that
some people (beginners, mainly) will meet more were-foos than
wargs, so the absolute death numbers must indeed be taken with a
grain of salt. The best numbers to judge should be taken from
players who are no beginners and regularly get at least to the
mid-game. Personally, as a quite experienced player, I never
died to a warg, while I have a couple of were-foo based deaths.

